			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Route IPC channels through to Mountain and unify event constants\n\nRoute eight VS Code workbench IPC channels — `scm`, `debug`, `tasks`, `auth`, `language`, `languages`, `process`, `browserViewGroup`, `watcher`, `env`, and `history` — through the ChannelRouteMap to Mountain's native handlers, replacing their all-stub entries. The `watcher` channel's `watch`/`unwatch` methods reach Mountain's `file:watch`/`file:unwatch` arms, enabling the IFileWatcherService.\n\nConcrete changes:\n- **TauriMainProcessService**: Add 11 new `ChannelRouteMap` entries; remove stale stub blocks for `update`, `browserViewGroup`, and `watcher` (which are now fully routed); fix `utilityProcessWorker.createWorker` from a never-settling Promise to `Promise.resolve(undefined)` to prevent language-detection service init hangs; tighten stub resolution to only intercept commands explicitly named in the stub object, so partially-routed channels like `process` still pass unknown methods to Mountain\n- **FilesService.Watch**: Replace dead-code path-verification pattern with proper `IPCService.invoke(Channel.FileWatch)` / `Channel.FileUnwatch` calls, returning a `dispose` that actually sends the `unwatch` command\n- **EditorService**: Use the `SkyEvent.EditorActiveChanged` constant (`sky://editor/active-changed`) instead of the hardcoded string `editor:activeChanged`, and capture the `listen` unlisten callback for proper subscription cleanup\n- **Channel registry**: Add `AuthValidateToken: \"auth:validateToken\"` to support Mountain-side token validation\n\nRemoves the disposition-tracking and `_DevLogForward` diagnostics from the stub path since routed channels no longer hit stub code by accident.",
			"SHA": "f7b0ce604af267552155df5d8216481a53c171d3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:37:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				924,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Enable IUpdateService channel route in TauriMainProcessService\n\nUncomment the `update` channel route mapping, connecting VS Code's `IUpdateService` IPC channel through the Tauri preload bridge to Mountain. This route was previously stubbed pending Mountain's update service implementation.\n\nAccompanying documentation updates:\n- Architecture.md: Add branded table header with Land logo and em-quad spaced heading, matching the README convention\n- DeepDive.md: Reframe opening sentence with Wind as the grammatical subject for clarity",
			"SHA": "8c4f08013d189d4bfb3446c1d9e8d6ccae7d66d3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:17:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				924,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Wind): Overhaul README with comprehensive architecture and feature documentation\n\nRewrite the Wind README from a terse overview to a detailed reference documenting the complete service layer architecture. The previous README covered only basic mechanisms; the new version enumerates all 40+ Effect-TS services, documents the codegen pipeline, adds security and compatibility sections, and provides a full project structure tree with autogenerated Workbench* bridge entries.\n\nKey additions:\n- Compelling project epigraph framing Wind's replacement of untyped Electron IPC with typed Effect-TS services\n- \"Key Features\" section with emoji headers covering Effect-TS architecture, Preload shim, typed IPC, codegen pipeline, Mountain RPC, file system provider, telemetry, and layer composition\n- \"Core Architecture Principles\" table mapping principles (Compatibility, Modularity, Type Safety, Abstraction, Integration) to their key components\n- \"Connection paths\" table documenting all four IPC pathways (invoke, listen, direct import, TAURI bridge)\n- Expanded project structure tree including all Workbench* generated bridge modules, Codegen subdirectories, and Documentation/ entry\n- \"Security\" section with six enumerated security layers (type safety, IPC isolation, sandbox, network restrictions, DI, telemetry privacy)\n- \"Compatibility\" table showing integration targets (Sky, VS Code, Mountain, Cocoon, Tauri)\n- Updated dependency table (replacing @tauri-apps/plugin-dialog with typescript) and funding acknowledgement section",
			"SHA": "93f2c2786695873cbab8fd625e7bed0971280641"
		},
